  "text": "A route people use to walk somewhere.\n\nAsk Grandma about the lantern flowers\n\nMara: needs to hear this arrangement.\n\nEven while, or despite the fact that.\n\nWas placed or supported on something.\n\nBakery directions and other controls\n\nAn answer to something someone said.\n\nExplore the garden’s lantern stories\n\nBring the seed to Grandma’s landing.\n\nBridge directions and other controls\n\nHelp me start with a prepared ending\n\nAny thing, without specifying which.\n\nNotice with the eyes, or understand.\n\nAt that time, or next in a sequence.\n\nA flat surface used to store things.\n\nHaving information or understanding.\n\nMake a liquid flow from a container.\n\nis expecting a different arrangement\n\nMake an idea clear by describing it.\n\nDirecting the eyes toward something.\n\nWhy does the flour need to stay dry?\n\nPut something to work for a purpose.\n\nRepaired something that was damaged.\n\nYour suggested ending, chosen by Sol\n\nNext to or at the side of something.\n\nHold something up or keep it steady.\n\nFitted openings that hold the posts.\n\nPip, Sol, Mara and Grandma are here.\n\nThe Torn Wing · Mara’s earlier story\n\nTell Sol the current gathering time.\n\nPip’s carried things and their pages\n\nAway from or no longer on something.\n\nFeeling grateful for someone’s help.\n\nIntroduces the reason for something.\n\nYou are Pip · Explore, talk and help\n\nHere, make music with an instrument.\n\nThe surface at the bottom of a room.\n\nA path or surface meant for walking.\n\nPulled tight without hanging loose.\n\nIs important or makes a difference.\n\nMost recent or final in a sequence.\n\nSol’s workshop is beyond the bench.\n\nSol’s prepared ending: Rina’s visit\n\nMoved toward or arrived at a place.\n\nEveryone has had a chance to share.\n\nDirected the eyes toward something.\n\ng-writing-workspace g-writing-show-",
